---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

import '@/styles/reset.css';
import '@/styles/variables.css';
import '@/styles/base.css';
import '@/styles/layout.css';
import '@/styles/components.css';
import '@/styles/pages/privacy.css';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy | Tekevol"
	description="How Tekevol collects, uses, and protects the information you share through our website, forms, and call scheduling.">
	<main id="main">
		<section class="legal-hero">
			<div class="legal-container">
				<p class="legal-hero__eyebrow">Legal</p>
				<h1 class="legal-hero__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
				<p class="legal-hero__meta">
					Effective date: November 3, 2026 &middot; Last updated: November 3,
					2026
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="legal-body">
			<div class="legal-container legal-layout">
				<nav
					class="legal-toc"
					aria-label="On this page">
					<p class="legal-toc__title">On this page</p>
					<ol>
						<li><a href="#who-we-are">Who we are</a></li>
						<li>
							<a href="#information-you-give-us">Information you give us</a>
						</li>
						<li>
							<a href="#information-collected-automatically"
								>Information collected automatically</a
							>
						</li>
						<li><a href="#cookies">Cookies</a></li>
						<li>
							<a href="#how-we-use-information">How we use information</a>
						</li>
						<li>
							<a href="#how-we-share-information">How we share information</a>
						</li>
						<li><a href="#data-retention">Data retention</a></li>
						<li><a href="#your-choices">Your choices and rights</a></li>
						<li><a href="#do-not-track">Do Not Track</a></li>
						<li><a href="#security">Security</a></li>
						<li><a href="#children">Children's privacy</a></li>
						<li><a href="#other-websites">Links to other websites</a></li>
						<li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
						<li><a href="#contact-us">Contact us</a></li>
					</ol>
				</nav>

				<article class="legal-content">
					<p class="legal-content__intro">
						This Privacy Policy explains what information Tekevol collects when
						you visit tekevol.com, fill out one of our forms, or book a call
						with us, and how we use and protect it. We keep it simple: we
						collect what we need to respond to you and run our business, and we
						don't sell your personal information.
					</p>

					<h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
					<p>
						Tekevol ("Tekevol," "we," "us," or "our") builds and manages
						websites for small businesses. This policy applies to tekevol.com
						and any forms or scheduling pages linked from it.
					</p>

					<h2 id="information-you-give-us">2. Information you give us</h2>
					<p>
						When you request a quote or contact us through our website, you may
						provide:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>First and last name</li>
						<li>Email address</li>
						<li>Phone number</li>
						<li>Company name and website URL</li>
						<li>Your trade or industry</li>
						<li>
							The service package you're interested in and whether you already
							have a website
						</li>
						<li>Anything you include in your message</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						When you book a call through our scheduling page, we collect your
						name and email address, along with the date and time you choose.
					</p>
					<p>
						If you email or call us directly, we'll keep a record of that
						conversation and the contact details you share.
					</p>

					<h2 id="information-collected-automatically">
						3. Information collected automatically
					</h2>
					<p>
						When you browse our website, our analytics, advertising, and CRM
						tools automatically collect certain information, such as:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Pages you visit and how long you spend on them</li>
						<li>
							How you interact with pages, such as the links and buttons you
							click and how far you scroll
						</li>
						<li>
							How you arrived at our site (for example, a search engine, social
							media, or a direct link)
						</li>
						<li>Your browser, device type, and operating system</li>
						<li>Your IP address and approximate location (city or region)</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						If you submit a form, the pages you viewed before and after
						submitting may be connected to your contact record so we understand
						what you were interested in.
					</p>
					<p>
						We may also record how you move through our site, such as mouse
						movements, clicks, and scrolling, so we can find and fix parts of
						the site that are confusing or broken. These recordings hide
						anything you type into form fields, and we don't use them to
						identify you.
					</p>

					<p>
						Our site also uses the Meta Pixel, which sends Meta information
						about your visit and actions on our site, such as submitting a form.
						If you use Facebook or Instagram, Meta may connect this information
						to your account.
					</p>

					<h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies</h2>
					<p>
						Cookies are small text files stored in your browser. We use them to
						understand how people use our site, which pages lead to inquiries,
						and how well our ads on Facebook and Instagram perform.
					</p>

