					<p>
						Our service providers may also set a small number of technical
						cookies needed for security and performance.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong>Managing cookies:</strong> You can block or delete cookies in
						your browser settings. Blocking cookies won't stop you from using our
						site or submitting a form. To opt out of Google Analytics on all websites,
						you can install the <a
							href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener"
							>Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a
						>. To control the ads you see on Facebook and Instagram based on
						your activity on other websites, visit your <a
							href="https://accountscenter.facebook.com/ad_preferences"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener"
							>Meta ad preferences</a
						>. You can also opt out of interest-based ads from many companies
						through the <a
							href="https://optout.aboutads.info/"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener"
							>Digital Advertising Alliance</a
						>.
					</p>

					<h2 id="how-we-use-information">5. How we use information</h2>
					<p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Respond to your questions and quote requests</li>
						<li>Schedule and hold calls with you</li>
						<li>Prepare proposals and provide the services you sign up for</li>
						<li>Send follow-up emails about your inquiry or project</li>
						<li>
							Understand which pages and channels bring people to our site, and
							how people use it, so we can improve it
						</li>
						<li>
							Measure how our ads perform and show our ads on Facebook and
							Instagram to people who have visited our site
						</li>
						<li>Prevent spam and misuse of our forms</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						If we send you marketing emails, every email will include an
						unsubscribe link.
					</p>

					<h2 id="how-we-share-information">6. How we share information</h2>
					<p>
						<strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong> We share it
						only with service providers that help us run our business, and only as
						needed for them to do that work:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<strong>HubSpot</strong> stores our contact records, processes form
							submissions, tracks website visits, and runs our meeting scheduler.
							See <a
								href="https://legal.hubspot.com/privacy-policy"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener"
								>HubSpot's Privacy Policy</a
							>.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager</strong> help us measure
							site traffic and form submissions. We don't send your name, email, or
							phone number to Google Analytics. Learn <a
								href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener"
								>how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a
							>.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>PostHog</strong> is a product analytics tool that helps us understand
							how visitors use our site, including which pages and buttons get the
							most use and recordings of how visitors move through our pages. Recordings
							hide anything you type into form fields. We don't send your name, email,
							or phone number to PostHog. See <a
								href="https://posthog.com/privacy"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener"
								>PostHog's Privacy Policy</a
							>.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Meta (Facebook and Instagram)</strong> receives information
							through the Meta Pixel about visits to our site and form submissions,
							which helps us measure and deliver our ads. Meta uses this information
							under its own policies. See <a
								href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/"
								target="_blank"
								rel="noopener"
								>Meta's Privacy Policy</a
							>.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Google Calendar and Google Meet</strong> are used to schedule
							and host calls you book with us.
						</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						We may also disclose information if required by law, to protect our
						rights or the safety of others, or as part of a business sale or
						transfer.
					</p>

					<h2 id="data-retention">7. Data retention</h2>
					<p>
						We keep contact information for as long as we need it to respond to
						you, work with you, and keep accurate business records. We
						periodically remove contacts we're no longer in touch with. You can
						ask us to delete your information at any time.
					</p>
					<p>
						Google Analytics data is kept for 14 months, then deleted
						automatically. PostHog and Meta keep the data they collect according
						to their own retention policies.
					</p>

					<h2 id="your-choices">8. Your choices and rights</h2>
					<p>You can ask us to:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Tell you what personal information we have about you</li>
						<li>Correct information that's wrong</li>
						<li>Delete your information</li>
						<li>Stop sending you emails</li>
						<li>
							Stop using your visits to our site for advertising on Facebook and
							Instagram
						</li>
					</ul>
					<p>
						To make a request, email <a href="mailto:support@tekevol.com"
							>support@tekevol.com</a
						>. We may need to confirm your identity before acting on a request,
						and we'll respond within a reasonable time.
					</p>

					<h2 id="do-not-track">9. Do Not Track</h2>
					<p>
						Some browsers offer a "Do Not Track" setting. There's no common
						industry standard for how websites should respond to it, so our site
						does not currently respond to Do Not Track signals. You can still
						control cookies using the options in the <a href="#cookies"
							>Cookies</a
						> section.
					</p>

					<h2 id="security">10. Security</h2>
					<p>
						We use reasonable measures to protect your information, including
						encrypted (HTTPS) connections and reputable service providers with
						their own security programs. No method of transmission or storage is
						completely secure, so we can't guarantee absolute security.
					</p>

					<h2 id="children">11. Children's privacy</h2>
					<p>
						Our website and services are intended for businesses and adults. We
						don't knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
						If you believe a child has given us information, contact us and
						we'll delete it.
					</p>

					<h2 id="other-websites">12. Links to other websites</h2>
					<p>
						Our site may link to other websites, such as our scheduling page or
						client sites we've built. We aren't responsible for the privacy
						practices of those sites, so please review their policies.
					</p>

					<h2 id="changes">13. Changes to this policy</h2>
					<p>
						We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we'll
						change the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. If the
						changes are significant, we'll make that clear on our website.
					</p>

					<h2 id="contact-us">14. Contact us</h2>
					<p>Questions about this policy or your information? Reach out:</p>
					<address class="legal-address">
						<strong>Tekevol</strong><br />
						Email: <a href="mailto:support@tekevol.com">support@tekevol.com</a
						><br />
						<!-- TODO: replace with your business mailing address -->
						<!-- [Business mailing address] -->
					</address>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>
